  "notes": "USAGE:\n{抱擁|ほうよう} is a literary and formal word. In everyday conversation, ハグ (from English \"hug\") or {抱|だ}きしめる (to hold tightly) are more common.\nCarries a more emotional and dramatic tone than ハグ. Frequently used in novels, news reports about reunions, and sports coverage.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {抱擁|ほうよう}する (to embrace)\n- {抱擁|ほうよう}を{交|か}わす (to exchange an embrace)\n- {固|かた}い{抱擁|ほうよう} (a tight embrace)\n- {熱|あつ}い{抱擁|ほうよう} (a passionate embrace)",
